PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — post-fill level-set pruning, upstreamable to
leap71/PicoGKRuntime.

Applied to vendor/PicoGKRuntime by scripts/fetch-deps.sh. Kept as a patch because
it modifies dependency source; no flag-level override exists.

U-SK05-b  The fills that walk a dense accessor over a bounding box
          (RenderImplicit, RenderLattice, ProjectZSliceUp/Dn) allocate a leaf for
          every 8^3 block they touch, including the blocks that end up uniformly
          +background or -background. The csg paths already end in pruneLevelSet
          (Composite.h, prune=true) and LevelSetFilter prunes its own output, so
          these three are the only unpruned producers — and every downstream op
          then iterates the slack. Measured reduction: RenderImplicit -68.1%,
          ProjectZSlice -36.1%, RenderLattice -5.5% of tree memory, with
          bit-identical raw levelSetVolume, bit-identical mesh-roundtrip volume
          and byte-identical STL output on every path.

Value-neutral: the prune is openvdb's pruneLevelSet restricted to nodes that hold
no active value AND whose values all share one sign (PruneSignUniform). Every
inactive voxel a fill writes is exactly +/-background, so the replacement tile
carries the value each voxel already had. Plain pruneLevelSet is NOT value-neutral
here: it signs every inactive node by its FIRST value, so a fill whose bounding
box cuts solid interior deeper than the band (-background meeting +background
with no band between) flipped whole 8^3/128^3/4096^3 regions to one sign. That
broke the JS-callback render against the tape render and upstream PicoGK, which
never prunes these fills. PruneSignUniform is public so src/pico-hash.cpp and
src/pico-zslice.cpp apply the same rule.

HISTORY — this patch used to carry a second change, U-SK05-a (merge-based CSG:
csg* replaced by the Merge.h operators under a DeepCopy tag, to avoid the eager
whole-operand deep copy). It was REVERTED: the multi-thread build silently and
nondeterministically drops geometry at every voxel size below 1.0 mm, and a
patch-level toggle matrix showed U-SK05-a necessary and sufficient while
U-SK05-b alone is bit-exact (bench/results/webgpu-v2/sk-0-p0-toggle-matrix.jsonl).
Whether the race lives in openvdb's TreeToMerge under DeepCopy or in how the
patch drove it is NOT established, and answering that is the precondition for any
re-attempt. Do not reintroduce the merge path without it.

